{"id":"NCT07500090","title":"A Phase 3 Efficacy and Safety Study of HBS-301 in Participants With Idiopathic Hypersomnia (IH)","official":"A Phase 3, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-Controlled, Efficacy and Safety Study of HBS-301 in Participants With Idiopathic Hypersomnia (IH) Followed by an Open-label Extension","summary":"This is a Phase 3, multicenter, randomized, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled clinical study to assess the efficacy and safety of HBS-301 in adult participants (ages ≥18 years) with idiopathic hypersomnia (IH).","conditions":["Idiopathic Hypersomnia"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"HBS-301 tablet"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Has a current documented diagnosis of IH per the International Classification of Sleep Disorders, Third Edition (ICSD-3) or Text Revision (ICSD-3-TR) criteria with confirmatory polysomnogram (PSG) with multiple sleep latency test (MSLT; and if applicable, a 24-hour PSG report or an actigraphy report with sleep log) on file that led to the diagnosis and was completed within the last 10 years.\n* Has EDS.\n* Has moderate to very severe symptoms of IH.\n* If taking a permitted chronic concomitant medication or supplement, including nonprohibited antidepressants or wake-promoting agents, must be on a stable dose for at least 3 months prior to Screening and agree to continue at that stable dose for the Double-blind Treatment Period of the study. As-needed use of any treatment that could affect daytime sleepiness (including but not limited to stimulants, modafinil, and armodafinil) used on an as-needed basis is not permitted.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Has hypersomnia due to another medical disorder.\n* Has a history of pitolisant use within 5 half-lives prior to Screening.\n* Has a primary diagnosis of psychiatric illness, including depression, that is not well controlled.\n* Has a history of moderate or severe hepatic impairment.\n* Has a body surface area (BSA)-corrected estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) \\<60 mL/min.\n* Has a known history of long QT syndrome or any significant history of a serious abnormality of the electrocardiogram (ECG).","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":248,"start":"2026-03-16","pcd":"2027-10","upd":"2026-11-13","sponsor":"Harmony Biosciences Management, Inc.","areas":["neurology"],"central":["Katie Wilmsen · 443-309-5556 · clinicaltrials@harmonybiosciences.com","Michelle Manuel · 847-903-4610 · clinicaltrials@harmonybiosciences.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Sleep Disorders Center of Alabama","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35213","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Joseph Wright · 205-599-1020 · jwright@sleepalabama.com"},{"f":"Springhill Medical Center","city":"Mobile","pr":"Alabama","zip":"36608","s":"R","lat":30.6944,"lon":-88.043,"c":"Kennedy Green · 251-278-6022 · kennedy.green@amr-clinical.com"},{"f":"Phoenix Medical Group LLC","city":"Peoria","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85381","s":"R","lat":33.5806,"lon":-112.2374,"c":"Daniel Kasenovich · 623-583-6542 · dkasenovich@phxresearch.com"},{"f":"West Coast Pulmonary & Sleep Disorders Center","city":"Lancaster","pr":"California","zip":"93534","s":"R","lat":34.698,"lon":-118.1367,"c":"Stephanie Nava · 805-483-1185 · snava@fomatmedical.com"},{"f":"Stanford Center for Sleep Medicine","city":"Redwood City","pr":"California","zip":"94063","s":"R","lat":37.4852,"lon":-122.2364,"c":"Sara Lomba · 650-799-1565 · slomba@stanford.edu"},{"f":"University of California San Francisco","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94107","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"Kyra Powers · 415-823-3227 · kyra.powers@ucsf.edu"},{"f":"Trial Site Solutions","city":"San Ramon","pr":"California","zip":"04583","s":"R","lat":37.7799,"lon":-121.978,"c":"Phil Strauss · 925-415-5353 · phil@sleepmds.com"},{"f":"Santa Monica Clinical Trials","city":"Santa Monica","pr"